  "slug": "cryo-structure-34d6",
  "summary": "Recent releases expand RNA, covalent ligand and peptide interaction resources with AlphaFold3 models and ML-oriented curation.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is infrastructure that organizes experimental and predicted 3D structural information for downstream modeling. RR3DD 2.0 expands RNA 3D structure classification to 15,764 chains, clustered by RMscore into 1,042 clusters and mapped to Rfam. CovPDB 2.0 grows to about 6200 covalent protein-ligand complexes and adds AlphaFold3 cofolding models with predicted cysteine ligandability. Propedia 26 updates a protein-peptide interaction database explicitly aimed at machine learning applications. RNAcomp2D differs in kind: it is a web tool that runs thermodynamic and deep learning secondary structure predictors and visually compares their outputs. The common emphasis is curated, structure-linked resources and comparison layers; the listed records do not show physics-based modeling itself, and benchmarking evidence is not given in the summaries.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
